    turnFlow: 'Deal and play are counter-clockwise. Deal size varies: 6 players dealer gives 8 each to the other five (dealer sits out); 5 players 8 each; 4 players 10 each; 3 players 13 each plus one to centre. First hand coins are trumps and the holder of the two of coins leads (mano). Later hands the last card dealt to mano is turned for trump (or with 3 players a centre card). Follow suit, beat if possible, trump if unable to follow. After winning a trick you may declare one king-horse combination (40 in trumps, 20 in another suit) before leading. At end of play, count points; losers are determined by point-order rules (e.g. with 5 taking tricks the 2nd, 3rd and 4th highest lose).',
